        "original_id": "ffee3c6e-2ea0-5091-93e4-aa1144dcde46",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Dances: Discofox, hustle\n- Films: Saturday Night Fever\n- People: John Travolta, John Badham, Karen Gorney, Donna Pescow\n- Places: Europe, United States, Brooklyn\n\nFacts:\n- Discofox evolved in Europe in the mid-1970s as a social partner dance and a rediscovery of the dance hold within an improvisational disco dance scene dominated by solo dancing.\n- Hustle emerged in the United States at approximately the same time that Discofox evolved in Europe.\n- Saturday Night Fever is a 1977 American musical drama film directed by John Badham.\n- Discofox and hustle were both greatly influenced by the film Saturday Night Fever.\n- Saturday Night Fever stars John Travolta as Tony Manero, a working-class young man who spends his weekends dancing and drinking at a local Brooklyn discothèque.\n- Saturday Night Fever also stars Karen Gorney as Stephanie Mangano, Tony Manero's dance partner and eventual confidante, and Donna Pescow as Annette, Tony Manero's former dance partner and would-be girlfriend.",
